# Modified 2026-10-19 (and 2026-10-30: two respawn entries for OCBM): the changes against LIVI are stated in this header.
# Derived from LIVI scripts/livi-link/common/rootfs/etc/inittab (GPL-3.0-or-later). Change: the console
# shell goes through cttyhack (job control on the real tty) and is a login shell (reads /etc/profile).
# The UART shell is unauthenticated: physical access to the pads is the credential.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::respawn:/bin/cttyhack /bin/sh -l
# Revision 8: the OCBM relay's watchdog and the OCBM overlay's long-running service (both idle unless OCBM
# is in use; README §7.0e). Their output goes to /run/log, never to the console.
::respawn:/usr/sbin/usb-mode watch
::respawn:/usr/sbin/ocbm-overlay service
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
